// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/catalog_write.t27 -- what an admin write may produce, and where the bound is
; This contract owns the WRITE side and nothing else: the displacement ceiling, the text
; ceilings, the immutability of the family key on update, and the closedness of the unit-status
; set the storage CHECK enforces. It owns no vocabulary at all. The two classes, the six bodies,
; the displacement bands and the publishable/forbidden field lists are bike_catalog.t27's; the
; four unit statuses and their names are availability.t27's; the money-absence discipline is
; pricing_honesty.t27's. All three are named below by ID, none is restated, and every decision
; that would need one of their tables arrives here as a boolean argument instead. Every number
; traces to src/api/bikes.rs, migrations/077_bikes.sql or migrations/078_bike_units.sql at the
; line its comment gives. ASCII only (L3), English identifiers only (LANG-EN).
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-20, citation counts RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21). src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs
; is 5802 lines, the largest source file in this repository -- the next is src/main.rs at 4599.
; Both figures re-verified 2026-09-21 and both unchanged.
; The count of contracts that cite it did NOT hold. This paragraph said TWO, availability.t27 and
; order_money.t27, and said both cite it for something it RENDERS. Measured over the 43-file
; corpus on 2026-09-21 it is FIVE besides this file: turbobaby/availability (:41, a unit status
; label), turbobaby/order-money (:97, a star count through the baht formatter) and
; turbobaby/order-status (:18, :212, :327, :332, the pipeline stepper) cite it render-side as the
; old sentence said; turbobaby/upload-media (:84 CALLER_SOURCE, :191, :464) and
; turbobaby/validation-bounds (:118 HONEST_PARSER_CALLER, :331) cite it INPUT-side, and two of
; those are declared constants naming the screen rather than passing citations.
; The conclusion survives the correction and is now checkable instead of merely asserted: neither
; input-side neighbour claims the write bounds, and each says so in its own header --
; turbobaby/validation-bounds writes "It owns no admin write bound" and hands them to
; turbobaby/catalog-write by ID, and turbobaby/upload-media writes that it owns "no catalog
; column bound". So the screen is cited by five contracts and owned by none of them. It is the
; screen every catalog write starts from, and the read contracts decline its side of the boundary
; on purpose, so the bounds an admin write must respect had no owner before this file.
; That is not a tidiness problem. Five shipped columns refuse a value the API accepts: the CHECK
; at migrations/077_bikes.sql:67 requires displacement_cc > 0 while src/api/bikes.rs:1040 admits
; the whole closed interval from 0, and the four money CHECKs at 077_bikes.sql:59-66 require
; > 0 while src/api/bikes.rs:1009 refuses only a value below zero. On each of those five, zero is
; admitted by the API and refused by the column, and src/api/bikes.rs:1157-1158 turns that refusal
; into a 500 with an EMPTY body, because the only database error the create handler translates
; into a sentence is a duplicate key. So the owner gets a blank failure for a value the form let
; him type. The gap is exactly one value wide per column and nothing in the tree pins the two
; floors together: a grep for the constraint name bikes_displacement_positive over src/, scripts/
; and tests/ returns nothing, while the unit-status set IS pinned, by
; the_four_statuses_match_the_check_constraint at src/api/bikes.rs:2493. One boundary is proved
; equal to its column and the others are not, and that difference is what this file makes
; checkable.
; --
; WHERE THE ISSUE IS REFUTED. A reader expects the write path to check the body value against the
; six styles bike_catalog.t27 enumerates. It does not. src/api/bikes.rs:1055 length-checks the
; field and nothing else, and migrations/077_bikes.sql:35-37 declares the column unconstrained
; with the reason stated in the migration: the shop adds body styles when it buys a bike, and a
; CHECK there would reject a real one at seed time. The six styles appear on the write path only
; as form options, in two identical controls -- the create form at
; src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs:1112-1121 and the edit card at 2447-2450 -- and a request made by
; hand meets neither. So this file declares the missing guard as a tripwire rather than
; claiming a check that is not there, and it declares no body vocabulary of its own while doing
; it. The displacement ceiling is refuted in the other direction: turbobaby/bike-catalog owns
; DISPLACEMENT_MIN_CC and DISPLACEMENT_MAX_CC and records both as measured extremes that are
; reported and never used as a bound, and the comment over its DISPLACEMENTS_CC argues that a
; clamp to today's fleet would reject the next machine the shop buys. (Both were cited here by
; line number until 2026-09-21; a line into a sibling goes stale the day that sibling is edited,
; so the owner and the declaration names carry it instead. Re-verified on that date: the two
; constants exist under those names and still say that.) That is correct for a read contract
; and it leaves the write ceiling ownerless, which is why the ceiling lives here.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It quotes no error message: the shipped rejections are Russian
; sentences rendered verbatim under the save button, so they are pinned by the line that produces
; them and never by their wording. It names no route, no HTTP verb and no admin identity: who a
; request is belongs to request_identity.t27, named below by ID, and every function here takes the
; write it is judging and never the sender of it. It publishes no rate, no
; deposit and no sale price: the five column NAMES below are the places a CHECK lives, and not one
; value from any of them appears here. It carries nothing from D14 -- no renter, handle, phone,
; key code, plate, debt, purchase cost or personal note, in a constant, a fixture or a comment.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-catalog-write;

pub const KIND : str = "catalog-write";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/catalog-write";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby admin catalog write bounds";

; --- Ownership edges ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl, which the gate rejects, so a
; cross-contract edge is a string naming the owner's ID and a test asserting the literal. These
; three are the vocabularies this file consumes and refuses to declare.
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_ID : str = "turbobaby/bike-catalog";
pub const REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/availability";
pub const REUSES_PRICING_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
; The fourth edge is not a vocabulary but a boundary: who may send a write is owned there, and
; nothing in this file asks who the sender is.
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
; What each edge supplies, as the abstract thing this file's functions actually take.
pub const CLASS_AND_BODY_VOCABULARY_INPUT : str = "membership boolean supplied by the catalog contract";
pub const UNIT_STATUS_VOCABULARY_INPUT : str = "membership boolean supplied by the availability contract";
pub const MONEY_ABSENCE_INPUT : str = "absence discipline owned by the pricing contract";
pub const WHO_MAY_WRITE_IS_NOT_THIS_FILES_SUBJECT : bool = true;

; --- Sources ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const WRITE_SOURCE : str = "src/api/bikes.rs";
pub const FAMILY_MIGRATION : str = "migrations/077_bikes.sql";
pub const UNIT_MIGRATION : str = "migrations/078_bike_units.sql";
pub const ADMIN_SCREEN : str = "src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-20";
